 The workshop now opens one relation as well as positions. Taking the turquoise collar from the hand to the head leaves the thirteen points in place and retains twelve connections, yet isolates the hand and makes a loop elsewhere. A count and an outline can conceal that change. The isolated point can still look like a hand while the graph no longer joins it to the body. The second collar makes a different reunion possible: the isolated hand can join the head directly. Connectivity can return without a return to the assigned anatomy. This is an invitation to investigate recognition and belonging, not a general claim that more connections mean freedom. The other eleven relations and the inventory remain authored; growing another joint still asks for another operation. The changed pose now survives the loaded visit and returns beside its starting arrangement in the final hall. The record keeps destinations and both arrangements of connections but leaves out the path of the hand. That new permission brings a further question about what remembering a change should mean.
 
 The earlier theoretical and design text is [preserved for further development](../../../doc/space/postcrisis-pass-2026-09-15/before/commons/maps/AdvancedLaboratory_Lab_Equipment_Simulation/critical.md). This encounter grounds the claim in the current primary artifact; it does not turn an illustrative scene into empirical evidence about people.
+
+## When a connection has a consequence
+
+The new ragdoll makes the earlier absence of force available as a comparison. Pull the gold hand and the elbow stays; pull the coral wrist and the elbow follows. On release, one body retains the pose while the other falls. This difference is produced by assigned mass, rigid parts, rotating joints and contact. It does not belong to the visible outline alone.
+
+A slump can look exhausted or comic without an emotional state in the program. That is a useful question for the viewer, not proof that every visitor reads it the same way. Conversely, the presence of gravity does not certify a natural body: the puppet's unrestricted joint angles remain a deliberate simplification. The comparison can ask which constraints make a gesture sustainable, and what another set would let a body do. Its falling state is not added to the persistent gold-body record.
